---
import HearthNavigation from './HearthNavigation.astro';
---

<header class="orientation-header">
  <div class="orientation-brand-row">
    <a class="orientation-wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Hearth and Code, return to Orientation">Hearth <em>&amp;</em> Code</a>
    <p>Independent research studio · operated by Scott Rallya (Cognitectus)</p>
    <a class="orientation-journal" href="/journal/">
      Field Journal <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
  <nav class="hearth-navigation" aria-label="Hearth and Code rooms">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/" aria-current="page"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span><strong>Studio</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/practice/"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span><strong>Practice</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/philosophy/"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span><strong>Philosophy</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/research/"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span><strong>Research</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/portfolio/"><span aria-hidden="true">05</span><strong>Portfolio</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/dossier/"><span aria-hidden="true">06</span><strong>Dossier</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/questions/"><span aria-hidden="true">07</span><strong>Questions</strong></a></li>
      <li><a href="/correspondence/"><span aria-hidden="true">08</span><strong>Contact</strong></a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>
</header>

<style>
  .orientation-header {
    background: var(--surface-elevated);
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  }
  .orientation-brand-row {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .orientation-wordmark {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .orientation-brand-row p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
  }
  .orientation-journal {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
  }
  .orientation-journal:hover {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
  }
  .hearth-navigation ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0 var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0 auto;
    max-width: 70ch;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .hearth-navigation a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
  }
  .hearth-navigation a[aria-current="page"] {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .hearth-navigation a:hover {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
  }
</style>

<main class="ec-studio-page">
  <article class="ec-studio-content">

    <header class="ec-studio-intro">
      <p class="ec-eyebrow">Hearth &amp; Code</p>
      <h1>An independent research studio for answerable systems.</h1>
      <p class="ec-studio-lede">
        Hearth &amp; Code is my public workbench for research, software, knowledge
        architecture, and policy thinking. The goal isn't to show everything I've done.
        It's to make the work legible enough that you can question it, use it, or
        build on it.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="ec-studio-section">
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        I'm Scott Rallya (online: Cognitectus). I work independently on systems where
        complexity needs to stay inspectable — AI governance, knowledge architecture,
        agent coordination, and public reasoning.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio runs on a single principle: <strong>every consequential claim should
        have a source, a scope, and a way to be challenged.</strong> That's the bar.
        Everything else follows from it.
      </p>
      <p class="ec-studio-link"><a href="/dossier/">→ Read my working profile</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="ec-studio-section">
      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <p>The site is organized in eight layers. Each layer has a different purpose and a different reading mode.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="ec-studio-nav" aria-label="Site navigation guide">
      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/practice/">Practice</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Methods, library, artifacts</p>
        <p>The working tools. Field cards, prompt techniques, research notes. If you want to <em>do</em> something, start here.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/philosophy/">Philosophy</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Epistemology, civic governance, AI literacy</p>
        <p>Position papers and framework essays. Where I argue for specific ways of thinking about complex systems.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/research/">Research</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Technical work, methods, reports</p>
        <p>The research programs and system work — Exocore, HCAN, ESS, Ember Circuit — with sources and artifacts.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/portfolio/">Portfolio</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Selected projects</p>
        <p>The projects themselves, organized by domain and purpose. What I'm working on and why.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/dossier/">Dossier</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Working profile</p>
        <p>How I think and work — my "Hearthside Meta-Architect" archetype. The personality behind the work.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/questions/">Questions</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Open inquiries</p>
        <p>Questions I'm actively investigating. No conclusions yet — just the live threads.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/journal/">Field Journal</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Published writing</p>
        <p>Essays, technical articles, and notes. The narrative thread of the work.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-nav-item">
        <h3><a href="/correspondence/">Contact</a></h3>
        <p class="ec-studio-nav-meta">Public return path</p>
        <p>How to discuss a project, offer a correction, or start a correspondence.</p>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <section class="ec-studio-section">
      <h2>Where to start</h2>

      <div class="ec-studio-start">
        <h3>If you're new here</h3>
        <p>Begin with <a href="/philosophy/ai-literacy/">AI Literacy as Developing Practice</a> — a position paper on how to think about working with AI systems. It shows you the kind of work this studio does.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-start">
        <h3>If you want to build something</h3>
        <p>Go to <a href="/practice/">Practice</a> for the method cards and prompt techniques. Then check <a href="/research/">Research</a> for the technical systems.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="ec-studio-start">
        <h3>If you want to understand the perspective</h3>
        <p>Read the <a href="/dossier/">Dossier</a> for the working archetype, then explore <a href="/philosophy/">Philosophy</a> for the deeper positions.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="ec-studio-footer">
      <p>
        This site is independently operated. No tracking. No visitor profiles.
        If something here is wrong or incomplete, <a href="/correspondence/">tell me</a> —
        correction is always welcome.
      </p>
    </footer>

  </article>
</main>

<style>
  .ec-studio-page {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-lg);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .ec-studio-content {
    /* Single article, clean reading flow */
  }

  .ec-studio-intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .ec-studio-intro .ec-eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .ec-studio-intro h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .ec-studio-lede {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .ec-studio-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .ec-studio-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
  }

  .ec-studio-section p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-link {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .ec-studio-link a {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .ec-studio-link a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .ec-studio-nav {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xl) 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .ec-studio-nav {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-item {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid #f3f4f6;
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-item h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-item h3 a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-item h3 a:hover {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-meta {
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm) 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-nav-item p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .ec-studio-start {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--signal-ember);
  }

  .ec-studio-start h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs) 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-start p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-start a {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .ec-studio-start a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .ec-studio-footer {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    color: var(--signal-gray);
    font-size: var(--font-caption);
  }

  .ec-studio-footer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ec-studio-footer a {
    color: var(--signal-ember);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .ec-studio-footer a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
